WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.136 --> 00:00:14.857
leaned over Mellis, concerned.

2
00:00:15.557 --> 00:00:17.318
Then she looked over at Zann.

3
00:00:18.038 --> 00:00:21.159
"She must be shocked by all of this," Perda said.

4
00:00:21.179 --> 00:00:25.561
"It was too much for her, especially after hours of hard digging."

5
00:00:25.581 --> 00:00:27.342
"Yeah. Look!

6
00:00:27.542 --> 00:00:29.383
The rain is stopping," Zann said.

7
00:00:30.003 --> 00:00:31.303
Perda lowered her umbrella.

8
00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:32.824
Zann was right.

9
00:00:33.332 --> 00:00:36.575
The pink downpour stopped as quickly as it had started.

10
00:00:37.115 --> 00:00:42.720
After a moment Perda and Zann were able to revive Mellis, though she seemed weak and disoriented.

11
00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:46.143
"We'll take you home," Perda told the other girl.

12
00:00:46.163 --> 00:00:49.185
"You should probably lie down for a while."

13
00:00:49.866 --> 00:00:51.967
Perda and Zann helped Mellis to her feet.

14
00:00:52.628 --> 00:00:54.650
"Let's leave the tools here," Zann said.

15
00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:56.171
"We can come back for them later."

16
00:00:56.811 --> 00:00:59.314
Perda nodded, putting an arm around Mellis.

17
00:00:59.954 --> 00:01:02.096
Zann did the same on the girl's other side.

18
00:01:02.836 --> 00:01:05.017
"Lean on us while we walk," Zann told her.

19
00:01:05.797 --> 00:01:08.738
Perda blinked as she realized what Zann had just said.

20
00:01:08.758 --> 00:01:11.278
"Walk?" She grinned.

21
00:01:11.298 --> 00:01:14.259
"We don't have to do that anymore.

22
00:01:15.039 --> 00:01:16.500
We can zap her home!"

23
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:18.060
Zann laughed.

24
00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.061
"Now I'm the one who's forgetting we can do magic again!"

25
00:01:21.461 --> 00:01:21.821
he said.

26
00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.022
He grabbed Mellis by the arm.

27
00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:24.982
"Got her?"

28
00:01:26.303 --> 00:01:28.723
"Yep." Perda took hold of her other arm.

29
00:01:29.763 --> 00:01:31.324
"Ready?" "Zap!"

30
00:01:31.792 --> 00:01:32.473
Zann shouted.

31
00:01:34.714 --> 00:01:39.897
Splash! The three of them landed in a large pink puddle in front of Mellis' house.

32
00:01:40.617 --> 00:01:44.400
Vilkor was standing outside, staring in confusion at the puddle.

33
00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:47.041
"Aah!" he screamed when he saw them.

34
00:01:47.622 --> 00:01:48.982
"Where did you kids come from?

35
00:01:49.543 --> 00:01:51.264
You shouldn't sneak up on me like that!"

36
00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:58.268
Perda immediately noticed that, aside from the pink rainwater, the magic energy hadn't reached this area.

37
00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:02.323
The landscape around the farm buildings was still drab and brown.

38
00:02:02.343 --> 00:02:07.127
"Maybe the magic only works near the well," she said to Zann.

39
00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:09.288
Zann was staring past her.

40
00:02:09.308 --> 00:02:11.971
"No, I think it's still coming," he said.

41
00:02:11.991 --> 00:02:18.696
"Look!" Perda turned and saw a wave of green rolling toward them over the scrubby fields.

42
00:02:19.577 --> 00:02:22.039
Vilkor saw it, too, and screamed again.

43
00:02:22.059 --> 00:02:25.622
"It's all right, Uncle," Mellis said weakly.

44
00:02:25.642 --> 00:02:28.424
"It's just, um, magic.

45
00:02:29.032 --> 00:02:30.573
It came out of the new well."

46
00:02:31.753 --> 00:02:33.734
"What are you talking about?"

47
00:02:34.674 --> 00:02:38.676
Vilkor narrowed his eyes, seeming to forget about everything else.

48
00:02:38.696 --> 00:02:41.537
"We just need water from that well!

49
00:02:41.977 --> 00:02:43.278
Didn't you find any yet?"

50
00:02:44.018 --> 00:02:45.839
"Not exactly," Zann said.

51
00:02:45.859 --> 00:02:48.460
"Instead of water, we struck magic energy.

52
00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.121
It's like your friend Zira's potions but better!"

53
00:02:51.141 --> 00:02:54.122
"You won't need a well now," Perda added.

54
00:02:54.142 --> 00:02:58.024
"You should be able to create all the water you need through magic."

55
00:02:59.508 --> 00:03:00.729
She hoped that was true.

56
00:03:01.429 --> 00:03:07.552
After all, she didn't know exactly how magic worked on Terrica or how good Terricans could be at

57
00:03:07.612 --> 00:03:08.252
performing it.

58
00:03:08.932 --> 00:03:13.874
Mellis had tried to create a glass of water and wound up creating an entire rainstorm.

59
00:03:14.555 --> 00:03:21.338
Perda thought again about Galvan, the world with magic energy so strong that a simple spell could have

60
00:03:21.518 --> 00:03:22.738
unpredictable results.

61
00:03:22.758 --> 00:03:26.780
"I wonder if Terrica will be like Galvan," she thought.

62
00:03:27.796 --> 00:03:30.577
"Don't be ridiculous," Vilkor said.

63
00:03:30.597 --> 00:03:33.018
"Zira's potions are one thing.

64
00:03:33.538 --> 00:03:40.381
But the sort of thing you're talking about is impossible His words trailed off as the wave of

65
00:03:40.481 --> 00:03:41.822
magic energy reached them.

66
00:03:42.442 --> 00:03:47.984
Grasses and other plants sprang up around their feet, and a flower sprouted right under Zing.

67
00:03:48.584 --> 00:03:51.606
Surprised, the little dragon jumped and shot flames at it.

68
00:03:52.146 --> 00:03:57.288
The flower collapsed in a pile of ash, but dozens more soon grew to replace it.

69
00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:04.206
Perda and the others took a few steps back as the pink puddle expanded into a small pond.

70
00:04:04.786 --> 00:04:10.247
The scrawny fruit trees in the orchard leafed out, and a flowering vine crept up the wall.

71
00:04:10.827 --> 00:04:14.769
It soon covered the farmhouse with sweet-scented pink blossoms.

72
00:04:15.449 --> 00:04:16.869
Vilkor watched all of it.

73
00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.710
"How can this be happening?"

74
00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:21.710
he cried, smacking his forehead in confusion.

75
00:04:22.371 --> 00:04:25.071
He rushed to the little kitchen garden near the house.

76
00:04:25.091 --> 00:04:27.192
"My cabbages!

77
00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:31.810
I nearly turned them back into the soil yesterday because they were so small and weak.

78
00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:33.130
But look!

79
00:04:33.671 --> 00:04:34.951
They're now ready to eat!"

80
00:04:36.272 --> 00:04:37.512
Zann scratched his head.

81
00:04:37.532 --> 00:04:41.634
"I guess the magic energy is helping everything, not just people," he said.

82
00:04:41.654 --> 00:04:43.835
"It doesn't work that way where we're from."

83
00:04:44.735 --> 00:04:46.036
"Where you're from?"

84
00:04:46.716 --> 00:04:49.237
Vilkor's eyes went sharp and curious.

85
00:04:49.257 --> 00:04:55.440
"Come to think of it, I don't believe you kids ever told me exactly where that is."

86
00:04:56.364 --> 00:04:58.165
Perda traded a glance with Zann.

87
00:04:58.905 --> 00:05:00.026
Should they tell the truth?

88
00:05:00.646 --> 00:05:03.427
Zann shrugged and opened his mouth as if to do so.

89
00:05:04.067 --> 00:05:05.428
But Perda spoke first.

90
00:05:05.448 --> 00:05:10.530
"Just a faraway area, where we have magic," she said.

91
00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:13.832
She waved a hand vaguely in the direction of the well.

92
00:05:13.852 --> 00:05:18.153
"Ah. The distant land beyond the mountains, eh?"

93
00:05:18.594 --> 00:05:19.294
Vilkor said.

94
00:05:19.314 --> 00:05:21.895
"I hear things are strange there indeed."

95
00:05:22.295 --> 00:05:23.976
He tapped his chin thoughtfully.

96
00:05:24.668 --> 00:05:28.611
"Zira never would tell anyone where or how she learned to make her potions.

97
00:05:29.332 --> 00:05:32.174
Perhaps she traveled to that part of Terrica in her youth."

98
00:05:33.375 --> 00:05:35.617
Zann shot Perda a surprised look.

99
00:05:36.317 --> 00:05:37.498
She knew what he was thinking.

100
00:05:38.159 --> 00:05:43.023
He was wondering why she didn't just tell Vilkor they were from a different world.

101
00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:48.347
But even though Mellis already seemed like a friend, Perda didn't quite trust Vilkor.

102
00:05:49.068 --> 00:05:54.252
After all, what kind of man would force his young niece to dig a well all by herself?

103
00:05:54.988 --> 00:05:57.549
Perda noticed that Mellis still looked pale.

104
00:05:57.569 --> 00:06:01.230
"Mellis needs to lie down," she told Vilkor.

105
00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.931
"She was caught in the stream of magic.

106
00:06:04.991 --> 00:06:06.331
We think it overcame her."

107
00:06:06.351 --> 00:06:08.812
"It did, did it?"

108
00:06:09.872 --> 00:06:12.393
Vilkor shot his niece a slightly sour look.

109
00:06:13.393 --> 00:06:16.995
"Or is she trying to get out of finishing that well?"

110
00:06:17.915 --> 00:06:18.655
Perda sighed.

111
00:06:19.195 --> 00:06:21.736
The entire world around him had changed.

112
00:06:22.284 --> 00:06:27.130
But Vilkor still didn't understand that he didn't need to worry about his silly well anymore.

113
00:06:27.731 --> 00:06:32.577
If they didn't do something to convince him, she was afraid he'd order poor Mellis back to digging

114
00:06:32.678 --> 00:06:33.218
right now!
